  "chunks": [
    {
      "category": "study_plan",
      "lang": "en",
      "text": "Interior Design (التصميم الداخلي) — Bachelor (BA) study plan 2025/2026, Faculty of Engineering & Design, Middle East University.\nThe degree requires 141 credit hours in total:\n- University requirements: 18 credit hours (compulsory)\n- University electives: 6 credit hours\n- Faculty requirements: 24 credit hours (group A: 6, group C: 18 — freehand drawing, computer design applications, aesthetics, history of art and architecture, basic design, psychology and sociology of design)\n- Area of study (major) requirements: 81 credit hours\n- Area of study (major) electives: 12 credit hours\nThere are no ancillary courses in this plan. Remedial courses are taken only when required and are not counted in the 141 hours.\nThe plan includes Field Training (6 credit hours, 420 training hours, after passing 90 credit hours) and a two-part graduation project."
    },
    {
      "category": "study_plan",
      "lang": "en",
      "text": "Interior Design study plan 2025/2026 — approvals and signatories.\nFaculty Council decision 01/06-2025/2026, adopted 06/11/2025. Deans' Council decision 06/15-2025/2026, adopted 30/12/2025.\nHead of Department: Dr. Qusai Mansour. Dean of the Faculty: Prof. Ayman Abdel Salam Awad. Director of Admissions and Registration: Mrs. Nadia Al-Bakri."
    },
    {
      "category": "study_plan",
      "lang": "en",
      "text": "Interior Design — design studios and digital courses in the 2025/2026 study plan:\nResidential Design (التصميم السكني), Commercial Design (التصميم التجاري), Administrative Design, Touristic Design, Planning Space, Furniture Design, Lighting and Acoustic Design, Sustainability in Interior Design, Model Making and Molding Industry, Interior Design Visual Presentation, Computer Aided Design I and II (with Computer Aided Design III and Simulation as electives), Materials in Interior Design and Technical Equipment for Buildings."
    }
  ],
